1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Hi, we're Space Monkeys.
Satellites have watched Brazil burn since 2000,

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:07,000
but MODIS and VIIRS count fire differently:
switch sensors and the record doubles in 2012.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
We built OrbitBurn: one harmonized fire record,
in MODIS units, from 2000 to today.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
Pick an area and the year
a decision took effect.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:22,000
OrbitBurn tells you if fire is rising or falling,
and how it changed, against all of Brazil.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,500
Built on open NASA data, honest about uncertainty,
for the people who manage the land.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:30,000
OrbitBurn · Space Monkeys · NASA Space Apps 2026
